  "caption": "Quinn fell in love with a new hill and climbed it every day for three weeks. Then came a tender spot on the inner knee, just below the joint.\n\nA few tendons attach there over a small bursa, and a sudden jump in load (more hills, more kilometres, a new surface) can irritate the area. Weaker hips or quads may add to it.\n\nWhat often helps: ease off triggers for a while, sleep with a pillow between the knees, strengthen quads and hips over 6–12 weeks, and rebuild walking or running gradually. Many people can keep running at a lower volume if it settles by morning.\n\nGet it checked if the knee locks, gives way, swells quickly, or isn't improving after a few weeks.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
